/-!
# Source-generated quantitative persistence windows

Every receipt in an arbitrary generated finite shell path carries its exact
positive trace mass

```text
Q = coefficientCarrierNormSq(receipt trace).
```

The actual Galerkin update supplies a cutoff-independent negative-one time
budget `B`.  This module lets the source data generate the concrete time

```text
τ = Q / (12 (2π)² selectedShellSq max(1, B))
```

and proves that at least `Q / 4` remains on the complete receipt support for
every `t ∈ [0, τ]`.  Thus the selected-shell frequency is paid exactly once
in the motion estimate and is available to cancel against the viscous
frequency weight in the next cumulative consumer.

No trajectory, time window, cutoff, budget witness, selected coordinate, or
target state occurs in the producer mouth.
-/

